From a2266afecbfa85671b8103ee460db2d93766b939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:51:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion,app): the lathe axis fit sets off-centre
 features aside

A keyway's or cross hole's normal lines miss the axis, and the plain
least-squares concurrency fit let their area drag the fitted origin: a
72-segment D20 shaft exactly on G54 with a short keyway fitted 0.15 mm
off and was refused with advice (move the work offset) that cannot help.

axis::fit now reweighs the plain fit (multiaxis/axis_robust.rs): facets
whose normal lines meet the candidate axis within the concurrency
tolerance are kept, the rest set aside, and the line and its direction
refinement refitted on the kept set until it settles; the refit must
still pass the full judgement on every facet. A part with nothing set
aside keeps its plain fit bit for bit (goldens unchanged); fewer than
half the answering area kept keeps the plain fit, marked untrusted.
axis::fit_report exposes the share and trust; the spindle law names the
set-aside share and keeps the move-the-offset advice for the misplaced
case only.

Fixes #71

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
