From aa15cc0ef2fe79dcfa1c8b27b11825fc7e382bbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:03:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app,motion): name the features a trusted lathe axis
 fit set aside

A trusted spindle-law pass with features set aside (keyways, flats,
holes, eccentric sections) no longer generates in silence: the op's
path carries a non-blocking note naming the share of the turned
(non-end-face) surface that is not turned, above a 0.05 % floor so a
plain revolve says nothing; one decimal, never "0.0%". The untrusted
refusal now says the reading is biased by off-centre features and
moving the work offset may not fix it. The 50 %-area / 8-facet refit
guard is documented as a backstop behind judge's 90 % share.

Refs #71

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
